        "mission_intent": "We need to develop a comprehensive incident information sharing specification for our SOC that aligns with the standards and exchange formats referenced in the NIST Computer Security Incident Handling Guide. Specifically, the specification should define how our team will structure and transmit incident data using the Incident Object Description Exchange Format (IODEF) as the baseline schema, with extensions for phishing report data where applicable, and should incorporate Real-time Inter-network Defense (RID) messaging transported over HTTP/TLS for automated sharing with our sector partners. The spec must also address how we integrate IDMEF for our IDS alert normalization pipeline and map relevant vulnerability findings using OVAL and SCAP so that incident reports include machine-readable configuration and vulnerability context. Include a frequently-asked-questions section aimed at end users, system administrators, and information security staff that explains their roles in incident response and how shared data is handled. The document should reference our existing XCCDF checklists for configuration baseline validation and define the retention, sensitivity marking, and dissemination controls for all outbound incident exchange messages. Please have a draft ready for review by the end of next quarter so we can pilot with our first two ISAC partners.",
